diff --git a/plans/INTEGRATION-CONTRACT.md b/plans/INTEGRATION-CONTRACT.md
--- a/plans/INTEGRATION-CONTRACT.md
+++ b/plans/INTEGRATION-CONTRACT.md
@@ -1,4 +1,18 @@
 # Prime Care VIP — Integration Contract
+
+# B4 read-side containment retirement — 2026-11-09 (Refs / Closes #403)
+
+Michael’s 2026-10-19 decision: patient chart reads no longer evaluate `ELATION_READ_ALLOWLIST`, `ELATION_FULL_SYNC_ENABLED`, claim-lifecycle `status`, or Hint/membership status. This amendment supersedes historical read-gate descriptions below ONLY for patient read functions; history remains intact. No merge/deploy authorized.
+
+- Every read requires `Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID token>` verified by `verifyPatientToken`, rejects its permissive sentinel, then resolves exactly one patient via the existing lowercased `firebaseUid` index. Each read additionally passes the token’s ORIGINAL `token.uid` to `resolvePatientForCaller`; the resolved document’s `authUid` must match exactly, including case. Missing/conflicting exact binding returns no chart (`AUTH_UID_MISMATCH`, 403; existing wrappers may label error status INTERNAL). No email lookup, new membership gate or client-selected self chart.
+- `getMyPatientRecord`: bound patient only, explicit demographic projection; existing suspension response preserved. Already had no Elation allowlist gate.
+- `getAppointments`, `getAllergies`, `getProblems` (conditions), `getMedications`: own resolved document ID is the ONLY Elation patient filter. Existing client chart selectors are ignored, not accepted as authorization; these remain self-only.
+- `getLabs`, `getImaging`, `getMedicalRecords`: subject-scoped `patients/{id}/labs` queries, fixed category and deleted=false. `getLetters`: subject-scoped letters with patientVisible=true and deleted=false. Existing guardian subject resolver, separate GUARDIAN_READS_ENABLED/ALLOWLIST, chart-backed delegation, fail-closed denial/no self fallback and subject echoes are unchanged; guardian reads remain off.
+- All three artifact modes independently reverify token + exact self binding + authorized subject, then require a nondeleted report reference under that subject and matching stored category before Storage, signing or repair. New/internalUid and legacy fallback paths stay subject-derived; hidden/module-disabled artifacts remain absent; TTL unchanged.
+- Existing audit-first behavior, explicit portal suspension and module/item visibility are preserved; billing inactivity does not suspend portal access. No new response fields. Retirement removes read-side NOT_IN_ALLOWLIST denials, including the shared artifact path.
+- Shared accessGate.js is BYTE-UNCHANGED. Discovery, auto-invite, provisioning, ingest, claim/hydration, backfill and refill/write callers retain their original gates and resolver behavior. Deploy workflow/env wiring, Firestore/Storage rules, CRM, Auth triggers and social flags unchanged. This change removes the read denial, not missing-cache hydration or provisioning containment; do not promise data that was never ingested.
+- CI: portal-enforcement-test exercises real Auth/Firestore/Functions using synthetic fixtures with full-sync false and empty read/ingest allowlists; per-path owner/forged-selector/UID mismatch/duplicate/unbound/token tests plus artifact reference/category isolation. B4 unit gate checks exact-case binding and unchanged non-read gate behavior.
+
 
 # Portal SendGrid receiver review amendment — 2026-11-09 (#559 / Closes #362)
 

